PARITY (web → native, faithful + complete)
  • Recharts <Legend> entries → per-series swatch + verbatim value label (web renders `{value}`).
  • Toggle source useChartHiddenSeries (HiddenSeriesState | null) → the model OWNS the hidden set;
    `toggle(key)` flips it (web `resolved.toggle`), forwards to the host (URL/localStorage persistence),
    and `reset()` clears it (web HiddenSeriesState.reset).
  • Hidden entry → dimmed (opacity 0.4) + strikethrough, aria-pressed=isHidden → spoken accessibility
    value "Hidden"/"Shown" + toggle hint.
  • web `resolved == null` → the `.passive` interactivity branch: static labels, no toggle, no dimming.
  • web `pickKey` (dataKey → payload.dataKey → value) → host supplies each entry's stable `id`
    (dataKey) + display `label` (value).
  • web `align` → ChartLegendAlignment over a wrapping Swift `Layout`; `verticalAlign`/`wrapperStyle`
    are Recharts layout pass-throughs = the embedding view's concern for a standalone surface.
  • P4 leaf axes added over the web body: loading skeleton, QueryError-peer retry, friendly empty
    state (default) / empty-payload withdraw collapse, stale chip + one-shot auto-refresh, offline
    chip. Every state renders — never a blank box.

